// The commentary box: every line the two commentators can say, in Italian, Romanian, Indonesian and English. Pure data. The sound of each line
// is made once by tools/make-voices.py from what clipsFor() returns here; a changed line is a new clip, the tool sees it by its text.
//
// A pool is what can be said about one thing. `voice`: 'a' or 'b' is one commentator, 'both' makes the line in both voices (for what
// the other one answers), absent alternates a and b line by line. `who`: the line is made once per driver, `{who}` is the name. `mood`
// is how it is spoken. Rules: nothing about deaths, victims, religion or real people, a disaster is a warning and a laugh at the
// mud, never at anyone. Fifi and Baileys are named like everyone, and no line is written about them but the bite.
